    std::cout << "Accessing shared resource..." << std::endl;
}

// Main method wrapped for unit testing
#ifndef UNIT_TEST
int main() {
    return 0;
}
#endif
```
**Expected Result:** No `main` is compiled, so the code focus shifts entirely to other testing functions or test harnesses.

